WEBVTT

00:04:57.625 --> 00:05:00.684
who has more status
or who has more accomplishments.

00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:03.726
I was really curious to hear
how you'd think about this.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.143
EP: So we can have
an interesting chat about power,

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.458
but --

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.851
AG: Are you going to
save that for later too

00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:13.684
or are we going to talk about it now?

00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:16.018
EP: That I can -- but it's so interesting.

00:05:16.042 --> 00:05:18.518
What you're highlighting
is the kind of the tension

00:05:18.542 --> 00:05:20.018
that comes, you know, from --

00:05:20.042 --> 00:05:21.309
this dynamic tension

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:23.768
that comes from the difference
in the discrepancy.

00:05:23.792 --> 00:05:25.768
I look at power a little bit differently.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.101
I would put it like this.

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:30.893
There is no relationship
that doesn't have a power dimension.